<details>
<summary>Exact original finding text</summary>

_🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Dispose can leak resources if a shutdown throws.**

If `server.shutdown()` rejects, the loop exits early. `releaseFixture()` then never runs, so the temp root is not removed. Remaining servers also stay open. Use `try/finally`, and settle all shutdowns first.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
   f.dispose = async () => {
-    closeReservations();
-    for (const server of helperServers.splice(0)) await server.shutdown();
-    await releaseFixture();
+    try {
+      closeReservations();
+      await Promise.allSettled(helperServers.splice(0).map((server) => server.shutdown()));
+    } finally {
+      await releaseFixture();
+    }
   };
```
</details>
